To calculate the cost of removing all the presents above the current present, we can use the following formula:
- If the current present is at the bottom of the stack, then the cost is $2 \cdot (n - 1) + 1$.
- If the current present is not at the bottom of the stack, then the cost is $2 \cdot (n - 1) + 1 - 2 \cdot (i - 1)$, where $i$ is the index of the current present in the list of presents Santa wants to send.

