<solution>
```python
def is_reachable(N, p):
    stack = []
    for i in range(N):
        # If the current element is already in the right place, move on
        if p[i] == i + 1:
            continue

        # Try to put the current element into the right place
        while stack and p[i] < stack[-1]:
            if stack[-1] != i + 1:
                return "No"
            stack.pop()

        # If we can't put the current element into the right place, use the operation
        if stack and p[i] == stack[-1]:
            stack.pop()
            stack.append(i + 1)
        else:
            stack.append(p[i])

    # If we've made it this far, the permutation is reachable
    return "Yes"
```

This solution uses a stack to keep track of elements that are out of order. It iterates through the permutation, trying to put each element into its correct position. If it can’t, it uses the operation to move it into place. If it can’t do that either, then the permutation is impossible to fix. If we’ve made it all the way through the permutation without failing, then the permutation is reachable.
